1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,000
In this video, we'll show you how to create and configure a new site in Burp Suite Enterprise Edition.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
A site is essentially just a representation of any website or web application that you want to scan.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:29,260
As a lot of the functionality and scan data is managed on a site-by-site basis, you'll need to create a site before you're able to launch any scans.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
So after logging in, hover over the sites menu and select add a new site.

5
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,000
First of all, you need to add a few basic details about your site. So we'll start out by giving it a name.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
This can really be anything you like, it's just something to help you identify the site later.

7
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:58,000
If you want to, you can add your site to a specific folder. As you can see here, I've got a European sites and a US sites folder in my site tree.

8
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:05,000
But if you're just starting out, you won't have any folders to add this to, so we'll just leave that blank.

9
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
In a production environment, you might have multiple different machines for running scans on.

10
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
In this case, you can use machine pools to control which machine is used to scan which site.

11
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:21,000
But again, as we're just starting out, we'll just assign this site to the default pool.

12
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Next, you just need to enter the main URL for your site.

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:39,000
This is the top level URL that you want to include in scans of this site, and it's where all of your scans will start from before crawling and auditing any other endpoints that are discovered along the way.

14
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:48,000
And that's really it in terms of the basic configuration. If you want, you can already scroll down to the bottom, click save and go and schedule some scans of this site.

15
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:53,000
But just in case, let's go over a few of the advanced options that are available.

16
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Under advanced options, you can enter a list of additional URLs that you want to include in the scope of this site.

17
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:08,000
This lets you pull in different domains or paths that all collaborate together to form a single application that you want to scan.

18
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,000
You can also specify any URLs that you want to exclude from scans.

19
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:19,000
You might do this, for example, to avoid scanning fragile functionality that might be broken by some of the more aggressive scan checks,

20
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:23,000
or you might just want to skip certain locations to avoid performance issues.

21
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:28,000
By default, all URLs are scanned using both HTTP and HTTPS.

22
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:37,000
But if you prefer, you can manually specify the protocol for each URL you list and select the option to scan using only your specified protocols.

23
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:41,000
If you want to scan functionality or endpoints that are only available to authenticated users,

24
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:47,000
you can specify application logins that Burp Scanner can use to log into the target site.

25
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:52,000
For simple login functions that are all on a single page and just require you to enter a username and password,

26
00:02:52,000 --> 00:03:05,000
you can provide sets of login credentials for Burp Scanner to use during the crawl and audit.

27
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:11,000
When Burp Scanner identifies a login form, it will attempt to log in using each of the sets of credentials that you provided.

28
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:24,000
For more complex login processes that use single sign-on, for example, you can use our browser extension to manually record yourself performing the login sequence and then upload it here.

29
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:30,000
In this case, Burp Scanner will use the script that the extension generates to replicate your actions during the crawl.

30
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:33,000
We'll cover recorded login sequences in more detail in a separate video.

31
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Scan configurations let you fine-tune virtually everything about Burp Scanner's behaviour, including what sort of checks it performs.

32
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,000
You can select a scan configuration each time you create a new scan,

33
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:48,000
but if you want you can specify a default configuration for this site so that it's pre-selected for you.

34
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:58,000
In this case, I'm going to create a quick scan that will crawl for a maximum of 10 minutes and only perform light active audit checks.

35
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:02,000
We'll cover exactly how scan configurations work in more detail in a separate video.

36
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Once you're happy with everything, just click save and your site will be added to the site tree.

37
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:14,000
You can see a list of all the sites you've already configured at any time by clicking the sites button at the top of the screen.

38
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:22,000
This shows all of the sites that you've configured so far, as well as a few key details such as the number of issues found by the most recent scan,

39
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:25,000
and some information about the current scan status.

40
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:31,000
As we touched on before, you can also group your sites into folders.

41
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:36,000
So as you can see here, I've got a European sites folder and a US sites folder.

42
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
How you group your sites is really up to you.

43
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:45,000
You could do it based on their geographical location like I've done here, or based on the development teams that work on them for example.

44
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Really just whatever makes sense for you.

45
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:57,000
To create a new folder, just click New Folder and give it a name.

46
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:03,000
You can drill down into any of your sites to view more information about them.

47
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:07,000
As we haven't run any scans yet, most of these tabs are empty.

48
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:10,000
So for now, let's focus on the details tab.

49
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:19,000
On the details tab, you can see all of the configuration options that you selected when creating the site, and you can edit them if you want to.

50
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:24,000
For the sake of an example, let's add this site to the folder we just created.

51
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:29,000
And as you can see, the site has now been added to the folder.

52
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:33,000
So now you know how to create a site in Books Weeks Enterprise Edition.

53
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:37,000
So now you can see the site in Books Weeks Enterprise Edition.

